# TypeScript & Code Quality Standards

## TypeScript Configuration
- Use TypeScript throughout the project
- Follow the configuration in [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json)
- Target ES2017 with strict mode enabled
- Use `@/*` path mapping for imports

## Code Quality Rules
- **Type Definitions**: Always prefer `type` over `interface`
- **File Size**: Keep all files under 250 lines of code
- **Comments**: Don't generate comments in source code by default unless explicitly requested
- **Imports**: Use absolute imports with `@/*` when possible
- **Error Handling**: Implement proper error boundaries and error states
- **Performance**: Use React 19 features appropriately (concurrent features, transitions)

## Best Practices
- Use modern React patterns (hooks, functional components)
- Implement proper loading and error states
- Follow Next.js 15 App Router conventions
- Use server components where appropriate
- Implement proper TypeScript types for all props and function parameters
- Use proper async/await patterns for Firebase operations

## Code Organization
- Keep components small and focused
- Separate business logic from UI components
- Use custom hooks for reusable logic
- Implement proper prop validation with TypeScript
- Follow the single responsibility principle

## Firebase Integration Types
Define proper types for Firebase data models as shown in feature specs:
- User profiles, rooms, messages, presence data
- Use Firestore Timestamp types appropriately
- Implement proper error handling for Firebase operations